# qkeee-erp.env — isolated ERPNext credential file for qkeee-erp-associate.
#
# Real location: $HERMES_HOME/plugin-data/qkeee-erp/qkeee-erp.env, mode 600,
# read only in the gateway by the qkeee-erp plugin
# (qkeee_erp.core.client's _qkeee_env_file_path() resolves it — never
# hardcode the path elsewhere). The old $HERMES_HOME/qkeee-erp.env is read
# only while the new file is missing; `hermes qkeee-erp setup` (step S1) moves
# it. Deliberately NOT the profile's main .env: it keeps these credentials
# physically separate from any LLM-provider secret, and no credential
# reaches a terminal or execute_code sandbox. See
# references/01-connectivity.md, "Credentials".
#
# Copy this file to $HERMES_HOME/plugin-data/qkeee-erp/qkeee-erp.env and fill in real values —
# out-of-band, on your own machine, never by having the agent read/cat
# this file or a command embedding these values back to you.
#
# <TAG> is the sanitized, uppercased form of an Instance tag (the plugin
# setting plugins.entries.qkeee-erp.settings names the active one). One file holds every tag's vars at once — add a
# new environment by appending its own BASE_URL/API_KEY/API_SECRET trio
# below, never by creating a second file or profile.

# --- Required, per tag ------------------------------------------------

# QKEEE_ERP_DEFAULT_BASE_URL=https://org.erpnext.com
# QKEEE_ERP_DEFAULT_API_KEY=changeme
# QKEEE_ERP_DEFAULT_API_SECRET=changeme

# --- Admin credential, per tag (system-admin writes + init-bot only) -----
# A SEPARATE key pair held by a System Manager account. Only the
# system_admin.* operations and hermes qkeee-erp init-bot's provisioning use it; every
# other read and write uses the everyday bot pair above, which must NOT
# hold System Manager. Leave unset on a tag where no system-admin write
# should ever happen — those operations then fail closed.
# QKEEE_ERP_DEFAULT_ADMIN_API_KEY=changeme
# QKEEE_ERP_DEFAULT_ADMIN_API_SECRET=changeme

# --- Optional, per tag --------------------------------------------------
# QKEEE_ERP_DEFAULT_ALLOW_INSECURE=1
# Tax-ID field a Supplier's KYC Address must carry, when it isn't one of
# gstin / tax_id / pan:
# QKEEE_ERP_DEFAULT_KYC_TAX_ID_FIELD=vat_no

# --- Optional, global ---------------------------------------------------
# Extra field names whose values are masked in audit payloads (comma-
# separated), on top of core.client.AUDIT_MASK_FIELDS:
# QKEEE_ERP_AUDIT_MASK_FIELDS=salary,ctc

# There is deliberately no REQUESTED_BY or ENV_CLASS var here — both were
# removed. `requested_by` is never a standing default (per-tag or
# otherwise): it's resolved fresh, on every call, from the live inbound
# channel identity (the chat/email sender's own work email); an Operator
# CLI run names it with --requested-by. Setting QKEEE_ERP_<TAG>_REQUESTED_BY in
# this file no longer does anything — qkeee_erp.core.client doesn't read it. See
# references/01-connectivity.md.

# --- Example second environment -----------------------------------------
# QKEEE_ERP_DEMO_ERP_BASE_URL=https://demo2.xyzorg.in
# QKEEE_ERP_DEMO_ERP_API_KEY=changeme
# QKEEE_ERP_DEMO_ERP_API_SECRET=changeme
